  "structure_method": "X-ray diffraction",
  "function_summary": "Aspartic protease essential for the life cycle of HIV-1 that cleaves newly synthesized Gag and Gag-Pol polyproteins at nine specific cleavage sites to produce mature, infectious virions. Without functional protease activity, viral particles remain immature and morphologically defective, completely lacking the ability to infect host cells.",
  "disease_relevance": "Direct therapeutic target for the treatment of Human Immunodeficiency Virus Type 1 (HIV-1) infection and Acquired Immunodeficiency Syndrome (AIDS). Inhibition of this enzyme prevents viral maturation and halts disease progression.",
  "quaternary_structure": "Homodimer of two identical 99-amino-acid chains (C2-symmetric)",
